courses.learning_outcomes:
By the end of the course, students should be able to

* comprehend and discuss selected texts related to science, technology and nature;
* interpret the essential characteristics of how human beings view nature;
* describe and analyse the societal implications of scientific explorations;
* identify and evaluate the relation between the developments in natural sciences highlighted in the course and their own lives; and
* analyse the scopes of application, achievements and limitations of highlighted scientific methods.

courses.course_syllabus:
A range of issues will be examined, addressed through six texts selected from *In Dialogue with Nature: Textbook for General Education Foundation Programme*, 3rd ed. (see “Section 8 – Required and Recommended Readings” below). The issues include the following:

* human understanding of the physical world;
* human understanding of the world of life;
* understanding of ourselves, especially the mind;
* reflection on science and its methodologies; and
* the relationship between humans and nature.
